[{:db/id "q-319372/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "e267c69c-11b0-56c9-8a03-72cacb05bb71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319372/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b8cd9a5f-5e9e-5780-86cc-fdfe1d030772" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-319372/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-319372/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-319372/field-2/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" :answer/id #uuid "3e87af07-bd78-5b6b-9782-ab45832e8cdd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319372/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "b12a7aba-a704-53eb-a3bb-01a5a157d455" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-319372/field-2/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" :answer-field/choices ["q-319372/field-2/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-319372/field-3/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "e1628abe-17c7-5e2a-b8c7-5edc553bd2e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319372/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e2b76ac-ebcf-5052-aa8a-690728e00b35" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-319372/field-3/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-319372/field-3/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-319372" :question/id #uuid "70daf951-b8fd-5de4-97d2-057221cebad2" :question/math-academy-id "q-319372" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]$\ngiven that $det(A)=7.$\n\n|  |  | $-1$ | {{field-1}} | $-1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{7}\\,\\,$ |  | $-11$ | {{field-2}} | $3$ |  |\n|  |  | $-4$ | {{field-3}} | $3$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 11 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -10 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -11 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -10 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -11 & -10 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -11 & -10 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-319372/field-1" "q-319372/field-2" "q-319372/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "50c01507-99a7-5328-8d74-c9e9bda51330"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-319372"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-319360/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "6b426850-7585-55cf-a00f-c1d0b4ed3bd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319360/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "6c8b1ad7-ae5d-5a9c-b30a-bc5db1f93281" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319360/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "52bf03b0-9bac-5c2f-a9fd-8c90c57bebf4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-319360/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-319360/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-319360/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-319360/field-2/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "9de0512a-1484-525b-9c9c-cef3345cb342" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319360/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "d756309d-2a5c-554e-a86c-33b8506f4a6e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-319360/field-2/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer-field/choices ["q-319360/field-2/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-319360/field-3/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "5cdd4878-68f0-53ee-8d7e-0b34858552ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319360/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "72fc41de-1bd9-5fc3-b455-52160f714d59" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-319360/field-3/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-319360/field-3/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-319360" :question/id #uuid "f6eb005e-ce68-5855-b912-c2ed17d9f4ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-319360" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}]$\ngiven that $det(A)=-5.$\n\n|  |  | $-17$ | {{field-1}} | $-1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\,$ |  | $12$ | {{field-2}} | $1$ |  |\n|  |  | $-3$ | {{field-3}} | $1$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-17 & -12 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-17 & 12 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-17 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 12 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-17 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 12 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-319360/field-1" "q-319360/field-2" "q-319360/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "50c01507-99a7-5328-8d74-c9e9bda51330"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-319360"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-18279"] :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+4|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(6-0)+2(0+1)+4(0+3) \\\\  & =6+2+12 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(-4-0) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21}=\\frac{1}{20}\\cdot 4=\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-104413/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "991cf3d7-9a3a-575a-a4eb-a4366a5031b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104413/selection/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" :answer/id #uuid "36d23edd-89b2-5c57-81c3-1bc7262b0304" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104413/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "812162fb-c7f0-56ba-9f1a-b802fbcd3d68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104413/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "74248aa0-3421-56e9-a8d1-c8e76c86da0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104413/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "5938be84-412c-5447-97b8-753cc52cd04b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104413/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "eed4e132-f4ea-5f11-bc84-39ba761d5d7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104413/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-104413/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-104413/selection/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" "q-104413/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-104413/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-104413/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104413" :question/id #uuid "b2dc099c-b9ae-5747-a320-990b6201e0cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-104413" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}A=|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(1-0)-0+(-1-0) \\\\  & =3+0-1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{32}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =(-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(0-1) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{23}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{32}=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104413/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c704e019-035f-5807-b02d-62b9cd44c1c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104413"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-319937/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "bbb13d0d-7884-58c6-8f9f-b3c955f7cb1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186283608 :answer-field/choices ["q-319937/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-9998/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "aae1cc10-a342-551a-ac41-43e21194cf45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9998/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "b58e780a-8b02-5e2a-86ec-74cdaffbf9ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9998/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "d518d397-3480-57b2-b673-1c1b9fac864e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9998/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "22a5220a-d62f-55f3-a136-23098b5baa5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9998/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "36c13751-b7fc-5464-86ac-2c23321cbbdb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9998/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d954f643-8863-56ba-8421-269518c65857" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-9998/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-9998/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-9998/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-9998/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-9998/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-9998/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-9998" :question/id #uuid "4551a234-86f0-5f56-a15a-28cd9a7837db" :question/math-academy-id "q-9998" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ k & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\nequals $-1.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ k & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-2(2k-0)+2(k-0) \\\\  & =-4k+2k \\\\  & =-2k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(4-2) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2k}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{12}^{′}=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{k} & =-1 \\\\ k & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-9998/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d79fb5d1-22a6-511d-90ca-7d66c540d172"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-9998"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-319859/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "604e9b23-51c3-5262-b35b-86f8a3816257" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319859/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "0fbf0f49-2d96-5783-b73d-91a17a0d1679" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319859/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6b25f54-747f-5260-9908-969b50f76fbf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-319859/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-319859/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-319859/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-319859" :question/id #uuid "4685104e-5c8e-5535-9bd4-12467257f628" :question/math-academy-id "q-319859" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ k & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nequals $-\\frac{1}{2}.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ k & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ k & 2\\end{aligned}|+(-1)|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ k & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\,(1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-1))-2\\,(0\\cdot 2-1\\cdot k)+(-1)\\,(0\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot k) \\\\  & =(2+1)-2\\,(-k)+(-1)\\,(-k) \\\\  & =3+2k+k \\\\  & =3k+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need ${c}_{12}^{t}={c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(2\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =-(4-1) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3k+3}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{3k+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we are told that ${a}_{12}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{2}$, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-3}{3k+3} & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -3k-3 & =-6 \\\\ -3k & =-6+3 \\\\ k & =\\frac{-3}{-3} \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-319859/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d79fb5d1-22a6-511d-90ca-7d66c540d172"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-319859"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-319434/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "4933487e-ae48-5963-ac90-702135f7876e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319434/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f4964ddd-44a7-5cc3-a80f-e165279c2020" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-319434/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-319434/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-319434" :question/id #uuid "27633a9f-8981-5e23-907e-da217010fa96" :question/math-academy-id "q-319434" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & k\\end{aligned}]$\nequals $\\frac{1}{3}$ and $det(A)=1-2k.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=1-2k\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}^{t}={c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(1\\cdot k-0\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(1-2k)}\\cdot (-k) \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{\\,2k-1\\,}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{12}^{′}=\\frac{1}{3}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k}{\\,2k-1\\,} & =\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 3k & =2k-1 \\\\ k & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-319434/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d79fb5d1-22a6-511d-90ca-7d66c540d172"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-319434"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
